---
import GscCaseStudyPage from "../../components/GscCaseStudyPage.astro";

const data = {
  slug: "metal-recycling-search-growth",
  metaTitle: "Metal Recycling SEO: +25% Clicks | Bright Forge",
  description: "An anonymized Google Search Console case study showing a metal recycling business adding 4,621 organic clicks as impressions rose 24.0%.",
  title: "A metal recycler added 4,621 organic clicks",
  breadcrumb: "Metal Recycling Growth",
  industry: "Metal recycling",
  period: "Reported 90-day comparison; visual trend 6 February to 3 August 2026",
  lede: "Organic clicks rose from 18,252 to 22,873 in the latest 90 days. Impressions grew by more than half a million, while average position moved the other way, from 7.0 to 9.0. The comparison shows more search exposure and more clicks. It does not show that every ranking improved, and we do not present it that way.",
  evidenceImage: "/images/case-studies/metal-recycling-search-growth-gsc-evidence.png",
  evidenceAlt: "Redacted Google Search Console performance visual showing 22,873 clicks for an anonymized metal recycling business.",
  metrics: [
    { value: "+25.3%", label: "Organic clicks", note: "18,252 to 22,873" },
    { value: "+519,291", label: "Impressions", note: "+24.0% search exposure" },
    { value: "22,873", label: "Latest-period clicks", note: "Google organic search" },
    { value: "90 days", label: "Comparison window", note: "Two 90-day periods" }
  ],
  evidenceHeading: "Search reach expanded and organic clicks grew with it",
  evidenceIntro: "The redacted presentation visual reports 22,873 clicks (+25.3%), 2,686,675 impressions (+24.0%) and average position 9.0, two positions worse than the prior period. Its trend runs from 6 February to 3 August 2026, with the comparison split marked at 6 May; exact comparison endpoints need the underlying export. Previous-period totals in the table below are retained from the published comparison. The redacted data does not show which queries account for the extra impressions.",
  problemHeading: "Large, fragmented demand needs coverage across more than one search theme",
  problem: [
    "Nobody searches for metal recycling with one perfect commercial term. People search by material, by service and by location, and a recycler is found for that variety only when it has enough relevant pages to match it.",
    "The client’s query set stays confidential, but the performance evidence clearly shows more search exposure and more clicks over the comparison window."
  ],
  readingHeading: "More visibility came with more clicks, but the average-position figure needs context",
  reading: [
    "Clicks increased by 4,621 and impressions increased by 519,291. Click-through rate remained effectively stable, moving from 0.84% to 0.85%. That is consistent with the site reaching a wider pool of searches without losing its ability to earn clicks.",
    "Average position moved from 7.0 to 9.0. That is not presented as a win. It can happen when a site begins appearing for a wider, more competitive query mix, and it can also mean established rankings slipped. The right next step is to separate the high-value pages and query groups and read each on its own, because one blended average cannot tell those stories apart."
  ],
  takeaways: [
    "A wider query footprint can add meaningful traffic even when the blended average position becomes less flattering.",
    "Search Console averages need page and query-level follow-up before they become an SEO diagnosis.",
    "Pair traffic growth with commercial-page and conversion analysis before claiming business impact. This page claims none."
  ],
  results: [
    { metric: "Organic clicks", before: "18,252", after: "22,873", note: "+25.3%, or 4,621 additional clicks" },
    { metric: "Impressions", before: "2,167,384", after: "2,686,675", note: "+24.0%, or 519,291 additional impressions" },
    { metric: "Average position", before: "7.0", after: "9.0", note: "Worse by 2.0 positions, requiring query-level review" },
    { metric: "Click-through rate", before: "0.84%", after: "0.85%", note: "Broadly stable while impressions grew" }
  ],
  boundary: "This case study uses anonymized Google Search Console data only. It reports Google organic-search performance for a 90-day comparison, as labeled on the visual, and deliberately retains the less favorable average-position movement. Client identity, queries, URLs, revenue and lead data are not published. We present it as a measured comparison, not a log of site work, and not as a promise of similar performance for another business."
};
---
<GscCaseStudyPage data={data} />
